Manage endpoint access to your Redis™ Database Instance through Public or Private Networks.

USAGE:
  scw redis endpoint <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  add         Add endpoints for a cluster
  delete      Delete an endpoint for a cluster
  get         Get an endpoint
  set         Set endpoints for a cluster
  update      Update an endpoint

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for endpoint
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw redis endpoint [command] --help" for more information about a command.
